  Copyright (C) 1999-2005 Id Software, Inc.
  Licensed under the GNU General Public License version 2 or later.
  https://github.com/id-Software/Quake-III-Arena

  Overbounce's player movement and collision code is a direct port of the
  Quake III Arena game source to TypeScript. The following files are derivative
  works of id Software's code and carry its copyright:

    src/physics/pmove.ts        <- code/game/bg_pmove.c
    src/physics/slidemove.ts    <- code/game/bg_slidemove.c
    src/physics/constants.ts    <- code/game/bg_local.h, bg_public.h
    src/collision/cm-load.ts    <- code/qcommon/cm_load.c
    src/collision/cm-trace.ts   <- code/qcommon/cm_trace.c
    src/collision/cm-patch.ts   <- code/qcommon/cm_patch.c
    src/game/damage.ts          <- code/game/g_combat.c
    src/game/missiles.ts        <- code/game/g_missile.c
    src/math/*                  <- code/qcommon/q_math.c

  The port is deliberately faithful, including behaviour that is generally
  considered buggy (overbounce, the strafe-jump maximum-speed bug, and the
  discarded slide clipping in the gravity path of PM_SlideMove). Reproducing
  these exactly is the entire purpose of this project.

